<div class="card" id="getting-started">
  <h2><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-idea"/></svg> Getting started</h2>
  <details><summary>Where do I start?</summary><p class="muted">With your path. Pick one of nine — creator, freelancer, coach or consultant, local service, shop, online store, physical product, software, or still figuring it out — and it decides what you are asked, which ten rungs you climb and which quests you get. Then answer about a dozen questions written for that path — your skills, your budget, and the hours left after work — and NoBossly draws your archetype, your real constraints and the territories where you hold an edge. Then <strong>you</strong> draft the idea, in your own words, and the advisor stress-tests it against your own fit test and a live market search. NoBossly does not hand you a list of business ideas to pick from; the direction is your call.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What is a path, and can I change it?</summary><p class="muted">A path is the kind of way out you are building: content creator, freelancer, coach or consultant, local service, brick and mortar, online store, physical product, software, or still figuring it out. It decides which questions you are asked, which number your idea is measured against, which quests you are offered, and what the ten rungs of your ladder are called. You can change it whenever you like &mdash; answer the questionnaire again and everything downstream re-fits. XP and levels you have already earned stay with you.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What is a subpath?</summary><p class="muted">The second question every path asks: what kind, specifically. A copywriter and a developer are both freelancers and need almost nothing in common next; a TikTok account and a blog are both creator businesses and are measured completely differently &mdash; 10,000 followers for one, 50,000 monthly visitors for the other. Your subpath sharpens the questions, the bar your idea is held to, and some of the quests you get. Every path has an "other" option if none of them fit.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Why is my Level 4 called something different to my friend’s?</summary><p class="muted">Because the rungs are named for the work. A plumber climbs Odd Jobber &rarr; Kitted Out &rarr; Signwritten &rarr; Quoting; a creator climbs Lurker &rarr; Poster &rarr; Publisher &rarr; Regular. Underneath they are the same ten stages, worth exactly the same XP, and no rung on any path can be bought with points &mdash; every one gates on something that happened in the real world. Where a gate would be meaningless for your path (a creator does not need to register a company to take a sponsorship) that path gets an equivalent of the same weight, never a free rung.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What is the coach, and what does it know?</summary><p class="muted">It is the AI, and the only reason it is worth asking is that it is not starting from nothing. It knows your path and your subpath, the rung you are on, the exact quest blocking the next one, the hours and runway you gave us, the number your path is measured by, your own fit test and which of its criteria your idea is failing, and what you did and did not finish last week. You can see the whole list at the top of the coach page. Asking it something never requires explaining your situation first.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What are AI credits?</summary><p class="muted">A monthly allowance that stops any one account running up an unlimited bill \u2014 drawing a Compass runs a live web search and reads your website, which is not free. Free members get 20 a month and can see the balance in their account menu; it refills on the 1st. On the Escape plan the ceiling is high enough that you should never think about it, and you are not shown a meter, because a plan you have already paid for should not make you ration anything. There are no per-report fees and no idea-by-idea charges on any plan. Your first Compass never costs credits at all, on any plan, even at a zero balance.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What is free and what is paid?</summary><p class="muted">Free: your path and subpath, your first Compass with its live market scan, drafting your idea and having the advisor stress-test it, one launch blueprint, the coach, a weekly reading list from the guides, and every one of the ten rungs \u2014 plus the forum, peer feedback, following, your feed and the Wins wall. The game is never behind the wall. Paid adds the things that only matter while you are still climbing: this week\u2019s plan, proof review, unlimited Compass redraws and blueprints, live demand evidence, AI sprints, tailored challenges and goals, a startup budget, and running your own group or collaboration.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How does following work?</summary><p class="muted">Follow anyone from their profile or the member directory and their real achievements show up in your feed \u2014 clearing a quest, reaching a rung, posting a win. Only real achievements: nothing lands there for logging in or posting in the forum, because a feed you learn to scroll past is worth nothing. Each rung is named for that person\u2019s own path, so you will see \u201creached Level 5 \u2014 First Invoice\u201d from a plumber and \u201cLevel 5 \u2014 Paid Creator\u201d from someone making videos. Blocking someone removes you from each other\u2019s feeds in both directions.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What is a launch blueprint?</summary><p class="muted">Pick an idea you love and NoBossly builds a complete launch plan: positioning, ideal customer profile, pricing, revenue projections, and a go-to-market checklist. Blueprints are part of the paid plan.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What are 7-day sprints?</summary><p class="muted">Sprints break your launch into focused weekly pushes with AI-planned tasks, daily check-ins, XP, and streaks to keep you accountable.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How do tasks work on the free plan?</summary><p class="muted">Free members can manage up to 8 open tasks at a time manually. Paid plans unlock unlimited tasks plus AI roadmaps that disperse tasks with deadlines automatically.</p></details>
</div>

<div class="card" id="plans">
  <h2><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-upgrade"/></svg> Plans &amp; billing</h2>
  <details><summary>What's included in the free plan?</summary><p class="muted">Your Compass, drafting your idea with the advisor, full community forum access, up to 8 manual tasks at a time, and your member profile with levels and badges.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What do paid plans add?</summary><p class="muted">Unlimited launch blueprints, live demand evidence on your ideas, AI roadmaps and automatic task dispersement, challenges, milestones, and collaborations &amp; teams. See <a href="/pricing">Pricing</a> for current rates.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How do I cancel my subscription?</summary><p class="muted">Go to <a href="/account">Account settings</a> → Subscription → End subscription. You keep full access until the end of your current billing period. Lifetime purchases never expire.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Is payment secure?</summary><p class="muted">All payments are processed by Stripe — NoBossly never sees or stores your card details.</p></details>
</div>

<div class="card" id="account">
  <h2><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-setting"/></svg> Your account</h2>
  <details><summary>How do I change my email or password?</summary><p class="muted">Both can be updated in <a href="/account">Account settings</a>. Email changes require confirming a link sent to both your old and new address.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What's the difference between a public and private profile?</summary><p class="muted">Public profiles show your full profile to everyone. Private profiles only reveal your username, level, awards and badges. Toggle this in Account settings.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How do I deactivate or delete my account?</summary><p class="muted">In Account settings: deactivating hides your profile and signs you out — logging back in reactivates it. Deleting schedules permanent removal after a 7-day grace period, during which you can cancel by logging back in.</p></details>
</div>

<div class="card" id="community">
  <h2><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-community"/></svg> Community</h2>
  <details><summary>Where do I meet other members?</summary><p class="muted">The <a href="/community">Community</a> forum is open to everyone — most people there are doing this around a job, same as you. Browse <a href="/members">Members</a> to see profiles, and message them directly.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How do collaborations and teams work?</summary><p class="muted">Paid members can create projects and invite members by username. Teammates can be assigned tasks on your board.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What are challenges and milestones?</summary><p class="muted">Challenges are timed pushes (30/60/90-day) pinned to your dashboard; milestones mark real-world wins like "registered my business" — both award XP and badges.</p></details>
</div>

<div class="card center">
  <h3>Still stuck?</h3>
  <p class="muted">Ask in the <a href="/community">community forum</a> — the team and other members are happy to help.</p>
</div>
